                            <comment id="16365458" author="zjffdu" created="Thu, 15 Feb 2018 12:18:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Tagar&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Tagar&quot;&gt;Tagar&lt;/a&gt; It works for me in both ipython and ipyspark.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12910732/12910732_screenshot-1.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16365646" author="tagar" created="Thu, 15 Feb 2018 14:43:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Jeff are you using Python 2?&lt;br/&gt;
It might be different in Python 3.&lt;/p&gt;



</comment>
                            <comment id="16369604" author="tagar" created="Mon, 19 Feb 2018 23:55:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;From &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/grpc/grpc/issues/14446&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/grpc/grpc/issues/14446&lt;/a&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;I can confirm that Python 2 gRPC doesn&apos;t accept unicode characters. 

The Python gRPC API accepts the&#160;string&#160;type, which in Python 2 is equivalent to the&#160;byte&#160;type. 

Applications should do any encoding if they are using unicode characters.&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
